##description	PhytoScope multi-species example: first genes of soybean chromosomes 1, 2 and 3
##provider	Phytozome Glycine max Wm82.a2.v1 (public annotation, illustrative subset)
##species	Glycine max
##assembly	Glycine max Wm82.a2.v1
#
# Soybean is the legume representative. This file is deliberately written in
# GTF rather than GFF3 to demonstrate that the framework is format-agnostic:
# the same parser core reads both dialects.
#
# GTF has no ##sequence-region directive, so PhytoScope infers the sequence
# span from the data itself; the published chromosome sizes are supplied
# separately by ExampleDataset so the axis reads in real megabases. Three
# chromosomes are bundled so the sequence selector has something to switch
# between. Attribute syntax is key "value"; with gene_id / transcript_id
# linking the hierarchy, and protein_id carried on the CDS rows.
#
